# Tests for the bed centre - the moves near the bed's rotation axis that
# are legal, those that are legal only slowly, and the ones that sit on the
# axis itself and need the bed angle scheduled around them.  The moves
# that are refused outright are in polar_singularity_refuse.test, which
# needs a file of its own because SHOULD_FAIL applies to a whole test.
#
# test/multi_axis/test_centre_path.py checks the plans these moves are
# turned into, and test_kin_6axis.c runs the same plans through the real
# step compressor.  This runs them end to end through klippy.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG polar_singularity.cfg

# Home.  The R sweep runs along y == 0 at a fixed bed angle, so it is
# radial by construction and does not turn the bed at all - which is why
# it may start from a radius of zero.
G28 X
G28 B
G28 Z
G90

# Well clear of the centre: untouched at any feedrate the machine has
G1 X80 Y0 Z10 F6000
G1 X80 Y40 F6000
G1 X40 Y80 F6000
G1 X0 Y80 F6000

# Chords that pass near the centre.  Each is held to 5 * r_min mm/s
# whatever feedrate is asked for, so the F6000 below arrives as 200mm/s
# at a closest approach of 40mm, 25mm/s at 5mm and 5mm/s at 1mm.
G1 X40 Y-30 F6000
G1 X40 Y30 F6000

G1 X5 Y-20 F6000
G1 X5 Y20 F6000

G1 X1 Y-10 F6000
G1 X1 Y10 F6000

# The same on the other side of the axis, and at an angle to it
G1 X-1 Y10 F6000
G1 X-1 Y-10 F6000
G1 X-15 Y-15 F6000
G1 X-15 Y15 F6000
G1 X15 Y15 F6000

# Just inside the refusal threshold: a chord passing 0.15mm from the
# centre needs 0.75mm/s, which clears the 0.5mm/s floor
G1 X20 Y20 F3000
G1 X0.15 Y-10 F6000
G1 X0.15 Y10 F6000

# A quarter turn at a comfortable radius, then a half turn taken the
# long way round rather than across the middle
G1 X50 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y50 F3000
G1 X-50 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y-50 F3000
G1 X50 Y0 F3000

# Rotating the head near the centre does not turn the bed, so it is not
# limited by any of this
G1 X2 Y-8 F3000
G1 B20 F600
G1 B-20 F600
G1 B0 F600

# Printing near the centre still works, just slowly
G1 X20 Y0 Z0.3 F1500
G1 X2 Y-8 E1 F1500
G1 X2 Y8 E2 F1500
G1 X20 Y8 E3 F1500

# On the axis.  Arrive from +x, work along the axis - the N in [0, 0, N]
# - and leave along +y.  The arrival parks a tenth of a micron short, on
# the +x ray, and the departure turns the bed on a small arc before it
# leaves, so the bed is never asked to step.
G1 X40 Y0 Z10 F3000
G1 X0 Y0 F3000
G1 Z50 F600
G1 Z10 F600
GET_POSITION
G1 B20 F600
G1 B0 F600
G1 X0 Y40 F3000

# Back to the centre and out again the way it came - no turn needed
G1 X0 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y30 F3000

# Leaving in the opposite direction to the arrival is a half turn
G1 X0 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y-30 F3000

# Straight across the centre on a travel move is routed through it,
# stopping on the axis while the bed turns
G1 X-40 Y0 F3000
G1 X40 Y0 F3000
G1 X0.003 Y40 F3000
G1 X-0.003 Y-40 F3000

# A travel move so close to the centre that it would have to crawl is
# routed the same way
G1 X-20 Y0.05 F3000
G1 X20 Y0.05 F3000

# Printing away from the centre after all of that
G1 X20 Y0 Z0.3 F1500
G1 X20 Y8 E4 F1500

GET_POSITION
M114
M84
